 },
 "short_version": [
  {
   "lead": "What's going right",
   "text": "FY26 revenue +90% to ₹2,184 Cr and Q1 FY27 +172% to ₹820 Cr, with operating EBITDA held at 13-15% and ROCE ~37-48%; order book plus L1 positions ₹3,355 Cr and a ₹10,410 Cr pipeline."
  },
  {
   "lead": "What to be sceptical about",
   "text": "Growth depends on lumpy government and neocloud AI orders; inventory days hit 110 and the company swung to ₹200 Cr net debt, with an enabling resolution to raise capital. Promoters sold ~4% in February 2026."
  },
  {
   "lead": "Price",
   "text": "109x trailing earnings and ~80x EV/EBITDA, against Kaynes (66x) and Syrma (88x), for a business with 13-14% EBITDA margins."
  }
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "id": "business",
   "title": "Company overview and business model",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Netweb designs and manufactures high-end computing systems in Faridabad under the Tyrone brand: AI GPU servers and clusters, HPC supercomputers, and private-cloud / hyper-converged systems, with its own software stack. About half its customers are government (India AI Mission, National Supercomputing Mission, research labs) and half enterprises and Indian cloud providers.",
     "src": "May call p.3"
    },
    {
     "type": "tiles",
     "items": [
      {
       "value": "62%",
       "label": "AI systems share of Q1 FY27 revenue"
      },
      {
       "value": "₹3,355 Cr",
       "label": "Order book + L1, June 2026"
      },
      {
       "value": "₹10,410 Cr",
       "label": "Pipeline (60% converts in 18-24 months)"
      },
      {
       "value": "~5%",
       "label": "Exports share of revenue"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "bullets",
     "title": "Where the profit comes from",
     "items": [
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Margins of 13-14% come from in-house design and integration rather than box selling.",
       "src": "Aug call p.8"
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Asset-light: gross fixed asset turnover ~44x; no major capex planned.",
       "src": "Aug call p.5"
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "Plans component stock ahead of orders, which has protected margins in the memory shortage.",
       "src": "Aug call p.10"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "bullets",
     "title": "What changed in 3–5 years",
     "items": [
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "IPO in July 2023; revenue from ₹247 Cr (FY22) to ₹2,184 Cr (FY26).",
       "src": null
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "AI grew from ~15% to 43% (FY26) and 62% (Q1 FY27) of revenue.",
       "src": "May call p.7"
      },
      {
       "lead": "",
       "text": "New 15,000 sq ft facility for dense liquid-cooled GPU racks.",
       "src": "May call p.10"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
